ios-image-tile-edge

`gpui_apple/shaders.metal`: the polychrome sprite fragment clamps its atlas sample to half a texel inside the sprite's tile. `img()` rasterizes an SVG at 2x; on a 3x screen (iPhone) it is drawn larger than its pixels, the edge pixels' samples fell less than half a texel inside the tile and the linear filter mixed in the neighbouring tile's edge: a grey 1px line down the left side of 收藏's empty-state picture, as tall as the image. Images drawn at 1:1 or smaller already sample at least half a texel in and are unchanged (the desktop at 2x draws these SVGs 1:1).

